[{:seon.task/name "landed-tells-the-sessions-it-unblocks"
  :seon.task/plan "Plan Stage 1.8 (root, 2026-11-14): when a landing completes what a task needed, the sessions waiting on it are told, so no session polls and none messages another about it. Who waits: the live agents (a model agent, or a Claude session's agent once sessions work through their agents) of the tasks whose :seon.task/needs name a task that just merged. seon.task/landed-messages [db ids] answers who and what: each such agent's key and a body naming what landed, the task it unblocks and the form that takes it, (my.branch/merge-main!); an ended agent, or a task nothing needs, tells no one. seon.task/landed-tx writes them as messages from the system, and the reconciler's merge (seon.reconcile :octopus-merged) carries them in the same write as the merge's outcome, whose write wakes each recipient (seon.reconcile/write). Only the reconciler sends (root, 2026-11-14: no new machinery on the Claude side; bin/land does not call it). Estimate: one seek of :seon.task/needs reversed per merged task, one per needing task's agent; one message entity each, in the merge's one write."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/a-merge-tells-the-agents-whose-tasks-need-it}}]
